if you like action movies and you also  like John restore ease that dig into one  key conceptual hook and its many  implications along the way the old guard  is a film for youth from how it wraps up  to where it might go next this is the  ending of the old guard explained here's  your warning spoilers ahead for the old  guard the chief threat of the old guard  is marek a pharmaceutical tycoon who  becomes convinced that Andy and her near  immortal crew are the key to opening up  all sorts of pathways to curing disease  slowing the aging process and perhaps  even stopping death Merrick has vast  financial resources tremendous tenacity  and the help of cop Lee's research he  also has Booker's help and with all of  that at his back he's very nearly able  to capture and incapacitate every single  member of the old guard of course by the  end of the film Merrick has fallen out  of his own skyscraper with an axe in his  neck so he won't be coming after them  again any time soon that said as Andy  notes near the end of the film it's  almost impossible to stay hidden in the  modern world they live in  if Merrick was able to track him down  and deploy his wealth to very nearly  caged them all who's to say an even  wealthier business tycoon somewhere  can't do the same particularly after  they learn about what Merrick went  through all it takes is one person with  knowledge of the team who's willing to  say what they know when we first meet  Nylund she's an American Marine just  trying to do her best who discovers  quite by accident that she's immortal  much of the film's emotional core is  devoted to denial coming to terms with  her abilities and the massive  implications they have including what it  means for her relationship with her  loved ones as the other members of the  old guard explained if she tries to keep  in touch with her family and stay with  them until they die they'll grow to  resent her they will never forget  hey now despair in their eyes still now  persists in her desire to keep in  contact with her family to the point  that Andi even relents and gives her  back her phone in the end nyle chooses  her new family of immortals but reveals  in the final scenes of the film that she  still has her phone and therefore still  has a lifeline to her family even though  Copley has promised to make it look like  she was killed in action though nyle  seems content with finding her way as an  immortal it's very possible she'll seek  out her family again even after her  family learns of her presumed death it's  possible she won't be able to resist and  will open a box that she finds very hard  to close from the beginning of the film  it's clear that the old guard values  their privacy and he goes so far as to  offer to take a photo for some tourists  just so she can delete a picture she  happened to be in the background of then  of course Copley reveals that he's been  doing research on them going back  decades  complete with photographs old ID cards  news clippings and much more as penance  for his attempts to sell them off to  Marek  she tasks Copley with becoming their new  eraser of sorts he will be in charge not  just of helping them coordinate new  missions but of erasing every trace that  they were there in the first place by  the end of the film the old guard has a  new and powerful layer of secrecy in  their corner though Marek is the chief  villain of the old guard he's not alone  in his journey to capturing the crew and  learning their secrets arguably the most  important ingredient is Booker's  betrayal Andi and her crew very nearly  go down because her best friend and  fellow immortal decides it's worth it to  turn them all over to medical  researchers in the hope that one day  they'll learn how to finally die by the  end of the film Andi has found new  purpose in life after her struggle with  Marek and while she shares a part of  that with Booker the group still votes  to punish him by exiling him from the  team 100 years Rita day they'll meet new  year  till they are alive but just as he's  preparing himself for a lonely century  Andy's old partner Gwyn tracks him down  presumably to use him to get to Andy  again  Booker already betrayed the old guard  once with the potential unstable  immortal now hunting him down will he do  it again  Gwen's return is brief so there's still  a great deal we don't know about her  what we do know is that she's been  through a lot  she suffered a kind of torture that  mortal humans can only imagine and it  probably hasn't done anything good for  her mental state there's no doubt that  she'll at least put Booker in a  difficult position  whatever her plans may be the members of  the old guard know they can die they  just never know when each time they go  down in a fight could be the last but  none of them has any idea what triggers  that final death or what the signs are  near the end of the film  Andy realizes that she has lost her own  grip on immortality  when Booker's shot to her stomach  refuses to heal though she's apparently  now vulnerable enough that she could be  killed  Andy is at peace by the end of the film  she sees her newfound mortality is a  trade-off for Niles emergence as the  first new immortal among them in ages  seeing her young sister in arms fills  her with a new sense of wonder and  seeing cop Lee's research into her past  reveals to her that she has a purpose  she can still serve while she lives so  with all that in mind how much longer  does Andy actually have left will she  aged conventionally and die in a few  decades  Booker seems to think that's the case  though she seems to know something we  don't  telling him to have faked is it possible  that her lingering gifts could prolong  her life or even make her somewhat  harder to kill than a normal human we  don't know but Andy's definitely not  done testing her limits the members of  the old guard know quite a lot about how  their immortality works they know that  it is finite they know that they dream  of each other when they're apart and  they know that they are rare what they  don't know is why they've been given  these strange gifts and others habits by  the end of the film Copley has shown  them why in the course of his research  into the old guard he discovers that  Andy and her crew have a ripple effect  on people they save on missions if they  rescue someone that person's descendants  will do something great in the world  creating a cumulative good  multiplies the longer they stay alive  she saves a life to three generations  later we reap the benefits this  discovery is perhaps the most important  driving factor in the entire film  because it confirms for Andi that she  still has something worth living for the  world might be getting worse but she has  a palpable power to make it better  and so the crew sets out at the end with  a renewed sense of purpose even though  they still don't have all the answers  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

